    {
      "id": "port-behavior",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Behavior",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Behavior",
        "body": "## Implemented behavior\n\nportDeclarations combines authored and synthetic declarations; graphNodeContract resolves Port presentation and glyphs. Graph navigation resolves an explicit exposed Port before falling back to the graph’s root landing behavior.\n\n## Known gaps\n\nUnifying Port presentation with Declaration Surfaces is not part of the current contract. Legacy inline presentation is readable but not a new authoring recommendation. See github://twilite-zone/public/tasks/declaration-surfaces/root.node.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNo additional decision is required to describe the behavior above. Changes to that contract require an explicit task; implementation gaps are not implied approvals.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSource (twilite repository):\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/portRelationshipHandles.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/portDeclarations.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/graphNodeContract.js`\n- `components/GraphEditor/utils/graphNavigationAddress.js`\n\nFocused tests (twilite repository):\n- `tests/portDeclarations.test.js`\n- `tests/dynamicPortDeclarations.test.js`\n- `tests/graphNavigationAddress.test.js`\n\nThese pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.",
